HST Office: Microsoft Office keyboard shortcuts in HST Writer, HST Sheets and HST Slides (owner decision 2026-11-04: on a conflict the Microsoft binding wins; docs/SHORTCUTS-MSOFFICE.md lists every binding and every displaced LibreOffice key).

- officecfg Accelerators.xcu, per module; macOS bindings follow Office for Mac (install:module="macosx"); a key used only on Windows/Linux is install:module="unxwnt". Values without install:module are not used for a key that has language variants with one (officecfg/util/alllang.xsl drops them), so T_MOD1 lists both platforms.
- Symbol keys are bound under both key codes (GREATER and POINT, LESS and COMMA, ADD and EQUAL, TILDE and QUOTELEFT, NUMBERSIGN and 3, COLON and SEMICOLON): GTK delivers the shifted symbol, other back ends can deliver the base key.
- sc inputhdl.cxx, tabvwsh4.cxx: Alt+Enter (Option+Return) starts a new line in a cell and Ctrl+Enter fills the selection, as in Excel (upstream: the other way round).
- sc cellsh2.cxx: Ctrl+T (.uno:InsertCalcTable) also works in a new workbook: the default table styles are generated with the drawing layer, created on demand here.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
